{
  "primer": {
    "branches": {
      "identity": {
        "branches": {},
        "effect": {}
      },
      "world": {
        "branches": {},
        "effect": {}
      },
      "runtime": {
        "branches": {},
        "effect": {}
      },
      "daemons": {
        "branches": {},
        "effect": {}
      },
      "modes": {
        "branches": {},
        "effect": {}
      },
      "threads": {
        "branches": {},
        "effect": {}
      },
      "entity": {
        "branches": {
          "thread": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one conversation: a user, in a mode, as turns; it holds buffers and its configuration in traits",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "buffer": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one screen on a thread: data a view draws, in a mime the renderers key on",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "turn": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one utterance of a thread: a role, its parts, provider metadata; the thread is the chain by createdAt",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "mode": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one program on a daemon: a type and slug, a manifest of traits, the buffers it mints; the runtime's own carry no daemon",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "daemon": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one installed package running on the runtime: its slug is its id; it owns modes, a dataset of symbols and literals, notes, users",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "user": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one person on the lighthouse: a slug, how they authenticate, their home and dock in traits",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "terminal": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one seat of a user: where they sit (a daemon, a thread) and how the chrome is docked",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "note": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "a remark hung on something — a literal, a buffer, a turn, a mode — by a user or a daemon; notes nest",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "view": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one compiled component of a mode: a slug, a mime, the file the client imports; a buffer pins views",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "file": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one file a mode serves: a path inside the mode, bytes on disk, their hash and integrity",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "intent": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "what a user wants from a mode: a named aim threads are opened for",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "literal": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one concrete thing of a daemon's dataset — a word, a card, a position — addressed by slug, described by its symbol",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "symbol": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one word of a daemon's vocabulary: a slug the literals are described with",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          },
          "activity": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "valence": "one running act — a hallucination — on a thread: its controller's status, its steps; never stored, dies with the process",
              "load": "lazy"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "tools": {
    "branches": {
      "fs": {
        "branches": {
          "tree": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "path",
                  "depth"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to a directory. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  },
                  "depth": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 5,
                    "default": 2
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "The directory tree under an absolute path. Ground here before reading: every mode's paths (source · mountpoint · files) come from mode_find. Example: { path: \"/home/operator/jdex\", depth: 2 }."
            }
          },
          "find": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "pattern",
                  "path",
                  "limit"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "pattern": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "JavaScript regex matched against file names. Example: \"\\\\.md$\""
                  },
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to the directory to search. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  },
                  "limit": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 100,
                    "default": 50
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Files matching a regex over the file name, searched under an absolute path; answers absolute paths. Example: { pattern: \"\\\\.md$\", path: \"/home/operator/jdex\" }."
            }
          },
          "read": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "path"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to the file. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  },
                  "range": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "from",
                      "to"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "from": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 1
                      },
                      "to": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 1
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Read a file at an absolute path. Long files come back cut at 16 kB with a note — pass range (line numbers, 1-based) for the rest. Example: { path: \"/home/operator/jdex/README.md\", range: { from: 40, to: 120 } }."
            }
          },
          "write": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "path",
                  "content",
                  "append"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to the file. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  },
                  "content": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The whole text to write, or the text to append. Example: \"# notes\""
                  },
                  "append": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": false
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Write or append a file at an absolute path. Parent directories are created. Example: { path: \"/home/operator/jdex/22 finance/22.04 notes.md\", content: \"# notes\" }."
            }
          },
          "stat": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "path"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to the file. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Size, modification time and format of one file at an absolute path. Example: { path: \"/home/operator/jdex/README.md\" }."
            }
          },
          "move": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "from",
                  "to"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "from": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to the file as it is. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  },
                  "to": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to where it goes. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Move or rename a file, both ends absolute; parent directories are created. Example: { from: \"/home/operator/jdex/draft.md\", to: \"/home/operator/jdex/22 finance/22.04 draft.md\" }."
            }
          },
          "delete": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "path"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute path to the file. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex/20-29 company\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Delete one file at an absolute path. Directories are refused. Example: { path: \"/home/operator/jdex/draft.md\" }."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "shell": {
        "branches": {
          "run": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "command",
                  "cwd",
                  "timeout"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "command": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The command, run through the shell. Example: \"ls | head\""
                  },
                  "cwd": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Absolute working directory. Example: \"/home/operator/jdex\""
                  },
                  "timeout": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1000,
                    "maximum": 120000,
                    "default": 30000
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "One-shot shell command in an absolute working directory. The output tail and the exit code come back; a nonzero code is information, not failure. Example: { command: \"ls | head\", cwd: \"/home/operator/jdex\" }."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "entity": {
        "branches": {
          "schema": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "entity": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Entity type from the no-argument listing. Example: \"buffer\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Ground yourself before querying. No arguments: every entity on this daemon with row counts and card fields — buffer, thread, turn, literal, symbol and whatever else it opened. With entity: its columns, relations, filter operators, repository extensions and the card projection. Returns { entities: [{ type, rows, card }] } without an argument, { schema: { entity, rows, columns, relations, operators, extensions, card } } with one. Example: { entity: \"buffer\" }"
            }
          },
          "find": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "entity",
                  "fields",
                  "limit",
                  "offset"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "entity": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Entity type — list them via entity_schema. Example: \"buffer\""
                  },
                  "where": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {}
                    },
                    "description": "MikroORM filter over the entity's columns and relations; operators $eq $ne $in $nin $like $gt $gte $lt $lte $and $or $not. Example: { thread: \"01a09010-13aa-778b-bce7-19c38f835337\", status: { $in: [\"PENDING\", \"ACTIVE\"] } }"
                  },
                  "fields": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string",
                        "const": "card"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "string",
                        "const": "full"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": "card",
                    "description": "card: the repository's lean projection (id, slug, traits unless it declares its own); full: every column. Example: \"full\""
                  },
                  "order": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "type": "string",
                            "const": "ASC"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "string",
                            "const": "DESC"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    "description": "Sort by column. Example: { index: \"ASC\" }"
                  },
                  "limit": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 50,
                    "default": 12,
                    "description": "Rows per page. Example: 20"
                  },
                  "offset": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "default": 0,
                    "description": "Rows to skip — pass next.offset back. Example: 12"
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Query any entity on this daemon — the buffers on a thread, a thread's turns, literals by slug. Rows come back as cards — the lean agent projection; fields full only when a card lacks something you need. Columns, operators and extensions via entity_schema. Page by passing next.offset back as offset. Returns { <entity>: [rows], total, next?: { offset } }. Example: { entity: \"buffer\", where: { thread: \"01a09010-13aa-778b-bce7-19c38f835337\" }, fields: \"full\" }"
            }
          },
          "count": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "entity"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "entity": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Entity type — list them via entity_schema. Example: \"buffer\""
                  },
                  "where": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {}
                    },
                    "description": "MikroORM filter, the same shape entity_find takes. Example: { thread: \"01a09010-13aa-778b-bce7-19c38f835337\" }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Count matching rows without loading them — cheap grounding before a find. Returns { count }. Example: { entity: \"buffer\", where: { thread: \"01a09010-13aa-778b-bce7-19c38f835337\" } }"
            }
          },
          "update": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "entity",
                  "where",
                  "trait"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "entity": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Entity type — list them via entity_schema.",
                    "examples": [
                      "literal"
                    ]
                  },
                  "where": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {}
                    },
                    "description": "MikroORM filter naming the one entity, the shape entity_find takes.",
                    "examples": [
                      {
                        "slug": "flamingo"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "trait": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {}
                    },
                    "description": "trait data by name, merged deep over what the entity holds",
                    "examples": [
                      {
                        "LABELED": {
                          "name": "Flamingo — six species"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "examples": [
                  {
                    "entity": "literal",
                    "where": {
                      "slug": "flamingo"
                    },
                    "trait": {
                      "LABELED": {
                        "name": "Flamingo — six species"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "valence": "Write trait data on one entity of this daemon — a literal's translation, a buffer's label. Pass the entity type, a where naming the one entity, and a trait patch keyed by trait name; the patch merges deep over the held data, a new name joins its traits. Find the entity first via entity_find. Returns { message, <entity>: [the entity] }."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "buffer": {
        "branches": {
          "update": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "id"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "id": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The buffer id. Example: \"01a0856f-425f-72b8-b36f-decc1bb2050e\""
                  },
                  "data": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {}
                    },
                    "description": "Data keys to merge over buffer.data; keys you omit stay. Example: { summary: \"Six species on four continents.\" }"
                  },
                  "source": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "New content for the file this buffer loads, whole. Example: \"# Q3 · final\n\nRevenue …\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Write a buffer — the shared working surface between you and the user. Pass the buffer id and a data patch; the patch merges over the existing data keys. For a content buffer pass `source` instead: the file it loads is rewritten, same row, new hash. This thread's id is in the runtime row of your context; its buffer ids come from entity_find { entity: \"buffer\", where: { thread } }, or from the thread section when your primer carries one. Returns { message, buffer: [{ id, index, status, mime, data, trait }] }. Example: { id: \"01a09010-18e0-736f-ad3f-a65b44d3fa43\", data: { summary: \"Six species on four continents.\" } }"
            }
          },
          "label": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "id",
                  "label"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "id": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The buffer id. Example: \"01a0856f-425f-72b8-b36f-decc1bb2050e\""
                  },
                  "label": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "name"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "name": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "The short display name the operator reads on the line — a subject, not a sentence. Example: \"Flamingo — six species\""
                      },
                      "description": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "One sentence on what the thing holds, for the tooltip and the list. Example: \"Range, diet and the six species, from Wikipedia and two field guides.\""
                      }
                    },
                    "$id": "Label"
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Name a buffer. The label is what the operator reads on the buffer's line in the chat and in the buffer list — set it when a buffer's subject is clearer than its name, or when the operator asks. Returns { message, buffer: [{ id, index, status, data, view, trait }] }. Example: { id: \"01a0856f-425f-72b8-b36f-decc1bb2050e\", label: { name: \"Flamingo\", description: \"Six species, range and diet\" } }"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "thread": {
        "branches": {
          "update": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "id",
                  "trait"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "id": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The thread id. Example: \"01a09010-13aa-778b-bce7-19c38f835337\""
                  },
                  "trait": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "patternProperties": {
                      "^.*$": {}
                    },
                    "description": "Trait data to merge, keyed by trait name. Example: { LABELED: { name: \"Q3 filings\", description: \"the filings correspondence\" } }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Write a thread's trait data — its configuration surface. Pass the thread id and a trait patch keyed by trait name (e.g. MASKED query data); each named trait's data merges over the existing value. This thread's id is in the runtime row of your context. Returns { message, thread: [{ id, phase, traits, trait, counter }] }. Example: { id: \"01a09010-13aa-778b-bce7-19c38f835337\", trait: { LABELED: { name: \"Q3 filings\" } } }"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "mode": {
        "branches": {
          "find": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "type": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "A mode type. Example: \"office\""
                  },
                  "slug": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "A mode slug. Example: \"vdex\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Every mode of this daemon with its paths on disk — source, mountpoint, files — as rows: the absolute paths fs_* and shell_run take. The first row is the daemon and its mountpoint. Narrow by type or slug. Returns { message }. Example: { type: \"office\" }"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "primer": {
        "branches": {
          "read": {
            "branches": {},
            "effect": {
              "input": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "nature"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "nature": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "A nature from the primer index. Example: \"guides/render\""
                  }
                }
              },
              "valence": "Reads one deferred section of your primer by its nature, as listed under [primer]. Returns { message }. Example: { nature: \"guides/render\" }"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}